Third-party data and services
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Camera data
  app/src/main/assets/osm/india_cameras.json is derived from OpenStreetMap.
  © OpenStreetMap contributors. Available under the Open Database Licence
  (ODbL) 1.0: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/
  Attribution and licence details: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
  That file is a Derivative Database and is made available under the ODbL.
  It is regenerated by tools/fetch_osm_cameras.py (also published here).

Map display
  Vector tiles and styles: OpenFreeMap (https://openfreemap.org), using
  OpenMapTiles (https://openmaptiles.org) schema and OpenStreetMap data.
  Rendering: MapLibre Native for Android (BSD-2-Clause)
  Copyright (c) 2021 MapLibre contributors; (c) 2018-2021 MapTiler.com;
  (c) 2014-2020 Mapbox. https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native
  The map shows a permanent "© OpenMapTiles © OpenStreetMap contributors"
  credit for the tile and data licences. Library licence texts (MapLibre with
  its bundled third-party notices, MapLibre Java/GeoJSON (MIT), MapLibre
  Gestures (BSD-2), the Apache-2.0 libraries) ship inside the app under
  app/src/main/assets/licenses and are shown in Settings → Open-source licences.

Community reports
  Reports a user chooses to publish are sent as public OpenStreetMap notes
  via https://api.openstreetmap.org and become OpenStreetMap data.
